WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:03.220
We can't afford just to tinker around the
edges,

00:00:03.220 --> 00:00:06.399
a tax credit here, a regulation there,

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:12.120
our fight is for big structural change.

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:16.470
Elizabeth Warren wants the federal government
to provide free healthcare for every American,

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:18.560
college for every student who wants it,

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:20.240
childcare for every parent,

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:22.300
and housing for low income families.

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:26.440
And she wants to pay for it all with a new
tax on the richest of the rich.

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:29.040
She calls it the Ultra-Millionaire Tax.

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:32.180
Skimming a bit more off the top of the bank
accounts of the ultra wealthy

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:35.280
might sound like a good deal for working and
middle class Americans

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:37.420
who feel like they're falling behind.

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:40.680
But the reality is that wealth taxes have
been tried before

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:42.920
and they haven't worked the way that Warren
promises.

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:44.000
Here's why:

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:46.780
Warren wants to levy a 2% annual wealth tax

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:50.510
on all households with a net worth of over
50 million dollars

00:00:50.510 --> 00:00:55.780
and a 3% annual tax on those households with
net worths over one billion dollars.

00:00:55.780 --> 00:01:01.440
All I'm asking for is a little slice from
the tippy tippy top.

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:06.160
A 2 or 3 percent tax on multi millionaires
and billionaires might not sound like much.

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:11.820
They got to pitch in two cents and two cents
on every dollar after that.

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:16.740
Wealth taxes are different than other taxes
like, say, an income tax or a sales tax

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:18.900
which tax money when it moves around.

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:23.460
A wealth tax on the other hand taxes the same
pot of money every year.

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:26.240
Meaning that over time it becomes smaller
and smaller.

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:28.360
It's essentially a tax on large savings,

00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:32.360
the money that investors and entrepreneurs
rely on to start new businesses.

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:36.900
But I do think a system that allows billionaires
to exist

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:42.760
when there are parts of Alabama where people
are still getting ringworm

00:01:42.770 --> 00:01:46.320
because they don't have access to public health,
is wrong.

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:48.780
Unlike Alexandria Ocasio Cortez,

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:52.320
Warren has never said that the existence of billionaires is immoral

00:01:52.330 --> 00:01:56.259
but her plan to tax two to three percent of
their wealth on an annual basis

00:01:56.259 --> 00:02:00.320
is clearly motivated at least in part by a
desire to reduce their wealth

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:03.840
and what she perceives as a power imbalance
in our society.

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:06.440
The economists who helped Warren design her
plan

00:02:06.440 --> 00:02:09.860
have said that the idea is to make rich people
less wealthy.

00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:19.280
In analyzing her plan, they wrote that:

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:28.240
It's not really about raising tax revenue,

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:31.280
it's about using government power to make
sure rich people have less.

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:38.020
-that much wealth is bad for our economy and
bad for our democracy.

00:02:38.020 --> 00:02:42.100
Warren has often pitched her plan as a way
to raise money from the ultra rich

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:44.820
to pay for more government benefits for everyone
else.

00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:47.100
And on that count, it's likely to fall short.

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:52.400
Warren says her tax plan will raise 2.75 trillion
dollars over a ten year period.

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:54.500
But other countries have tried wealth taxes

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:57.720
and found that they raise far less money than
expected.

00:02:57.720 --> 00:03:02.340
In 1990, there were twelve OECD nations with
wealth taxes similar to Warren's.

00:03:02.350 --> 00:03:04.000
Today only four remain.

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:09.140
In Scandinavia of course healthcare is a right,
higher education is free.

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:14.140
Despite the tendency of politicians like Bernie
Sanders to hold up Denmark and Sweden

00:03:14.140 --> 00:03:18.290
as paragons of Democratic Socialism that the
US should emulate,

00:03:18.290 --> 00:03:22.299
the reality is that both nixed their wealth
taxes in the 1990s

00:03:22.299 --> 00:03:26.250
because too many rich citizens were pulling
their money out of the country.

00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:30.049
This capital flight resulted in lower rates
of entrepreneurship

00:03:30.049 --> 00:03:32.040
and relative economic stagnation.

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:34.440
Not only did the wealth tax hurt the economy,

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:37.280
it didn't even raise the money it was supposed
to.

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:39.250
When Sweden eliminated it's wealth tax

00:03:39.250 --> 00:03:42.670
it had virtually no effect on government finances.

00:03:42.670 --> 00:03:46.180
France tried a wealth tax for more than a
decade starting in 2000.

00:03:46.180 --> 00:03:49.980
It helped push an estimated 42000 millionaires
out of the country.

00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:52.420
They didn't pay the tax, they just left.

00:03:52.420 --> 00:03:55.140
What Warren wants to get around the capital flight
problem

00:03:55.140 --> 00:03:58.780
by taxing the money no matter where in the
world it's located.

00:03:58.780 --> 00:04:04.780
And imposing a 40% exit tax on anyone who
wants to renounce his or her citizenship.

00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:07.480
We're going to be out there countin' them
and watching them.

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:11.909
What we built right into the plan was far
more sophisticated

00:04:11.909 --> 00:04:15.920
and more investment in the enforcement.

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:18.460
Warren's plan relies on hiring more IRS agents

00:04:18.460 --> 00:04:22.700
partly to deal with the complexity of evaluating
total individual wealth.

00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:26.920
But throwing more tax collectors at the problem
isn't going to change the fact

00:04:26.930 --> 00:04:30.160
that the wealthy are very good at protecting
their money.

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:34.910
By offshoring it or by putting it into unique,
hard to value assets like artwork.

00:04:34.910 --> 00:04:37.800
Austria is one of the countries that used
to have a wealth tax.

00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:42.580
One of the reasons the country ended it was
because the cost of enforcement was so high.

00:04:42.580 --> 00:04:44.560
Based on it's failure in other countries

00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:47.040
and her vague proposals for addressing those
failures,

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:50.240
there's no compelling evidence that Warren's
Ultra Millionaire Tax

00:04:50.250 --> 00:04:52.320
will raise the revenue she claims.

00:04:52.320 --> 00:04:56.000
The wealth tax is best understood not as a
targeted revenue raiser

00:04:56.000 --> 00:05:00.890
but as a symbolic declaration of opposition
to the existence of out sized wealth

00:05:00.890 --> 00:05:02.320
regardless of how it was obtained.

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:05.940
What I want is I want these billionaires to
stop being freeloaders.

00:05:05.940 --> 00:05:10.500
Warren has described the Ultra Millionaire
Tax as a tool for addressing inequality.

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:13.320
But really it's just a presidential candidate's
way of saying

00:05:13.320 --> 00:05:16.920
'I oppose the existence of very rich people'

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:18.540
She could have just said it.

